  "title": "DGCA Orders Probe Into Death Of Air India Express Pilot",
  "publication_date": "2025-04-18T16:21:22Z",
  "summary": "India's aviation regulator, the Directorate General of Civil Aviation (DGCA), has ordered a formal probe into the death of an Air India Express pilot. Detail is scarce due to an access error on the source page. The investigation is expected to examine operational, medical and safety factors. Authorities have not released further information pending inquiry.",
  "content": "The Directorate General of Civil Aviation (DGCA) has ordered a formal investigation into the death of a pilot employed by Air India Express, according to the headline of the original report.\n\nAt the time of publication, the source content was not accessible and returned an \"Access Denied\" error, showing the following reference and links: Reference #18.8f014017.1785212034.5954f46 and https://errors.edgesuite.net/18.8f014017.1785212034.5954f46. No additional details about the circumstances of the pilot's death, timing, or immediate cause were available from the inaccessible page.\n\nDGCA probes typically review a range of factors, including aircraft maintenance and technical records, pilot duty and rest schedules, medical history and toxicology where applicable, cockpit voice and flight data recorder information if relevant, and compliance with operational procedures. The regulator may also coordinate with the airline, local law enforcement and medical authorities as part of its fact-finding process.\n\nGiven the limited publicly available information, the timeline for the DGCA inquiry and any preliminary findings remain unclear. Air India Express and DGCA statements were not present in the original, inaccessible report. Further updates are expected as the investigation proceeds and official statements or a final report are released.",
