  "markdown_content": "## Incident Details\\n\\nThe Directorate General of Civil Aviation (DGCA) has ordered a formal investigation into the death of a pilot employed by Air India Express, according to the headline of the original report.\\n\\n## Source Access Issues\\n\\nAt the time of publication, the source content was not accessible and returned an \u201cAccess Denied\u201d error, showing the following reference and links:\\n\\n> Reference #18.8f014017.1785212034.5954f46  \\n> https://errors.edgesuite.net/18.8f014017.1785212034.5954f46\\n\\nNo additional details about the circumstances of the pilot\u2019s death, timing, or immediate cause were available from the inaccessible page.\\n\\n## What a DGCA Probe May Include\\n\\nDGCA probes typically review a range of factors, including:\\n\\n* Aircraft maintenance and technical records\\n* Pilot duty and rest schedules\\n* Medical history and toxicology where applicable\\n* Cockpit voice and flight data recorder information if relevant\\n* Compliance with operational procedures\\n\\nThe regulator may also coordinate with the airline, local law enforcement and medical authorities as part of its fact-finding process.\\n\\n## Current Status and Next Steps\\n\\nGiven the limited publicly available information, the timeline for the DGCA inquiry and any preliminary findings remain unclear. Air India Express and DGCA statements were not present in the original, inaccessible report. Further updates are expected as the investigation proceeds and official statements or a final report are released.",
